  "explanation": "What the regime had to show for twenty-one years by 1983 was an inflation of 239 per cent, and the Diretas Já movement grew alongside it — the first protest at Abreu e Lima on 31 March 1983, then Goiânia, then Pacaembu. The direct election was refused and the electoral college met anyway under no coercion, which is what a regime does when it has lost the argument rather than the vote.",
